--- !u!114 &8392623517172611859
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7423595288053701735}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e8569f1993f8e724180f9d6effcaca6f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  slotName: {fileID: 7711577342761821782}
  slotDescription: {fileID: 6336556172752738994}
  BacteriaPurple:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 2025946648285971660}
    button: {fileID: 2432886015474906302}
    name: Bacteria Purple
    description: 'Bacteria Purple is a resilient and unpredictable microorganism
      that represents a higher-level threat compared to common bacteria, characterized
      by its ability to survive longer under pressure and disrupt the balance of
      its surrounding environment. It moves with irregular patterns that make it
      difficult to anticipate, forcing defenders to stay alert and adapt their strategies
      rather than relying on fixed placements or single attack types. '
  BacteriaRed:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 8106605614358078059}
    button: {fileID: 4522702596427753448}
    name: Bacteria Red
    description: Bacteria Red is a fast spreading bacterial enemy that represents
      highly aggressive pathogens capable of multiplying rapidly and overwhelming
      their environment when left.
  Fungi:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 8283956535950751658}
    button: {fileID: 1962311643236862873}
    name: Fungi
    description: Fungi is a kingdom of living organisms that plays a vital role in
      maintaining balance within ecosystems, primarily by acting as decomposers that
      break down dead organic matter into simpler
  Virus:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 8645365087351766091}
    button: {fileID: 1655161808747248314}
    name: Virus
    description: Virus is a microscopic infectious agent that cannot carry out life
      processes on its own and must invade a living cell to survive and reproduce.
      It consists of genetic material, either DNA or RNA, enclosed in a protein coat,
      and sometimes surrounded by a lipid envelope, allowing it to attach to host
      cells and hijack their internal machinery.
  Protozoa:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 8756076850458666530}
    button: {fileID: 4732942665252285622}
    name: Protozoa
    description: Protozoa is a group of microscopic, single-celled organisms that
      belong to the kingdom Protista and are commonly found in water, soil, and inside
      other living organisms as parasites or symbionts. They have diverse shapes
      and structures, can move using flagella, cilia, or pseudopodia, and obtain
      energy in various ways, such as ingesting organic matter or absorbing nutrients
      from their environment.
  Helminth:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 5755659573892703082}
    button: {fileID: 4138026983991364248}
    name: Helminth
    description: Helminth is a parasitic worm that lives inside a host organism and
      depends on the host for survival, growth, and reproduction, often causing various
      health problems in humans and animals. These organisms include several major
      groups such as roundworms, tapeworms, and flukes, which can infect the digestive
      system, blood vessels, or other tissues, leading to symptoms ranging from mild
      discomfort to severe malnutrition and organ damage.
